<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13088" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολ-ίτευτος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without political
				constitution</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολιτεία</span>), of
			nations, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1327b26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not fitted for public affairs, unstatesmanlike,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				31
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπατεία, λόγοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Crass.</u>
				12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.1034b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>withdrawn from public life, private,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1098d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>not in current use,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.7a
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
